                    <physDesc>
                        <objectDesc>
                            <supportDesc>
                                <support>
                                    <p>A large slab of coarse grey-brown stone. Intact and finished along the upper edge, intact but lightly damaged on the right edge, intact below; broken on the left side. The rear is roughly finished. The stone is thickest at the top, thinnest lower left.</p>
                                    <material ana="#material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Docimian" type="stone.marble" subtype="Docimian" resp="#Coccato" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/66.html">Medium-grained, homogeneous, grey, calcitic, smelly marble, likely Docimian. Optical microscopy: heteroblastic fabric with fine-grained areas. Digital microscopy: heteroblastic fabric (identification based on pXRF, digital microscopy, XRD, optical microscopy, stable isotopes analysis)
<placeName type="provenance">
 <ref target="https://www.geonames.org/12207392/iscehisar-bucagi.html">Bakakale</ref>
 <location>
  <geo>38.86194,30.75028</geo>
 </location>
</placeName><note> Petrographic imagery at <ref target="https://iiif.csad.ox.ac.uk/viewer/isicily/ISic000097">https://iiif.csad.ox.ac.uk/viewer/isicily/ISic000097</ref></note></material>
                                    <objectType ana="#object.plaque" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/259">plaque</objectType>
                                    <dimensions>
                                        <height unit="cm">48.3-48.7</height>
                                        <width unit="cm">45</width>
                                        <depth unit="cm">6.1-7.5</depth>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </support>
                                <condition/>
                            </supportDesc>
                            <layoutDesc>
                                <layout>
                                    <p>The text appears centered on the stone (uneven right margin, left margin missing). Line 1 is largest, with line 5 also given prominence by larger size than 2-4 and slightly greater spacing. The final three lines are smaller and less regular.</p>
                                    <rs ana="#execution.chiselled" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1">chiselled</rs>
                                    <damage/>
                                </layout>
                            </layoutDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote xml:id="h1">
                                <p>Tall letters, showing some narrowness/compression in the module; occasional use of ligature and hedera, with a distinctive form of the letter G. Note that the final three lines appear to be in a different hand, less regular, with a different interpunct, differences notable in e.g. E, G and R.</p>
