            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#JP">
                <p>To [---]a Procula, daughter of Lucius... [(name)] Plaetorius, son of Spurius, of the Claudian tribe, quaestor, aedile, duumvir, ... [(name) --]ius Galeo, son of Quintus, of the Quirina tribe, to whom the decurial order decreed aedilician honours, [---]a Longina, daughter of Lucius. [(name)] Proculus, of the Claudian tribe, quaestor four times, prefect pro duumvir, duumvir quinqennalis, military tribune of the Legio VI Ferrata. </p>
            </div>
            <div type="commentary">
                <p><!--commented out pending revision-->
                    <!--Must be before 194 AD, b/c the Lev.VI Ferrata acquires titles fidelis constans after this date. Includes Plaetorius, quaestor, aedile and dummvir; Galeo, honorary aedile; Proculus, quaestor (four times), deputy duumvir, duumvir quinquennalis, tr.mil. in Leg.VI Ferrata (prior to eq. career?). ae Luci filiae Proculae | - - -Spurii filio Claudia tribu Plaetorio, quaestori, aedili, IIviro, - - -Quinti filio Quirina tribu Galeoni cui ordo decurionum ornamenta aedilicia decrevit - - -ae Luci filiae Longinae - - -filius Claudia tribu Proculus, quaestor IV, praefectus pro IIviro, IIvir quinquennalis, tribunus militum legionis VI Ferratae. cf. Wilson (1988b: 151 with n.207).--></p>
            </div>
